<title>USA: Pa. law means $12 mln funding hit to SEPTA -- paper.</title>
<headline>Pa. law means $12 mln funding hit to SEPTA -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania's new utility deregulation law includes a provision that will eliminate as much as $12.3 million in state funding for the Southeastern Pennsylvania Transportation Authority next year, the Philadelphia Inquirer reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The cut would come from the agency's capital budget and results from a projected decline in revenue from a tax on utility real estate. The budget problem will last for only one year, however, state officials said.</p>
<p>Statewide, the loss of revenues from the tax will total about $17.6 million, the paper said.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
